# Throwaway Vite mode for LOCAL-ONLY visual review (run: vite --mode demo).
# Blanks every backend URL so the app runs in local-stub mode off the seeded
# INITIAL_STATE — no Supabase login gate, no writes to any live backend.
# `.env.<mode>` overrides `.env.local` in Vite's precedence order, so this wins.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_EMAIL_BACKEND_URL=
VITE_TWILIO_BACKEND_URL=
VITE_FORMS_BACKEND_URL=
VITE_PUSH_BACKEND_URL=
# No *_STUB flags are needed here. The quotes / integrations / team / twilio adapters infer
# their localStorage stub from the build's Vite mode (import.meta.env.MODE === 'demo') plus
# the blank backend URLs above, and that stub dead-code-eliminates from a production build
# (CS-010, CS-038; see app/src/lib/demoMode.js). VITE_FORMS_STUB is retired (the Forms
# module was removed 2026-09-19). The VITE_*_STUB flags remain only a DEV-ONLY opt-in for a
# NON-production build (e.g. to force a stub in CONNECTED dev from app/.env.local); a
# production build ignores them.

# Marketing demo mounts the SPA under /polishpoint/ (vite base + router basename).
VITE_BASE_PATH=/polishpoint/
